SUMMARY:Trials and Truth: A History of Witchcraft
DESCRIPTION:Category: ‘Quin Chat\nPrice: Free\nAvailability: 13 spots lef
 t\nStatus: You are Confirmed\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/
 events/206949\n\n5:30PM Reception\, 6:00PM Discussion\n\nIn a seasonal ode
  to witchcraft\, join us for a thought provoking exploration tracing the m
 yths\, origins\, and histories that have shaped its place in a Western Eur
 opean cultural lineage\, a lineage that runs through to the Americas and i
 nto the present day. Building on last year's Trials & Truth\, which examin
 ed the Salem Witch Trials\, Professor Julie Walsh returns to take the conv
 ersation beyond local lore\, exploring the European roots of the image of 
 the witch\, its enduring stereotypes\, and the complex relationship betwee
 n belief\, skepticism\, and the social consequences of believing the worst
  about your neighbors. The evening will delve into the origin story of th
 e medieval witch\, what this story reveals about power\, fear\, freedom\, 
 and social justice. \n\nJulie Walsh is the Whitehead Associate Professor 
 of Critical Thought\, Associate Professor of Philosophy\, and Director of 
 the Newhouse Center for the Humanities at the Wellesley College\; she spec
 ializes in early modern philosophy\, theories of freedom\, and the history
  of witchcraft. She will be in conversation with Liza Oliver\, Associate P
 rofessor of Art History and Director of the Pluralism Initiative at Welle
 sley College\; she specializes in the intersections of art\, colonialism\,
  and cultural history. Together\, they will offer members a fresh perspect
 ive on the historical roots and ongoing social impact of European ideas of
  witches\, witchcraft\, and evil. \n\n*This event is complimentary and re
 served for members only. Complimentary light bites and refreshments will b
 e served. We kindly ask that all cancellations be made at least 24 hours p
 rior to the start of the event.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/206949
CATEGORIES:‘Quin Chat
END:VEVENT
